  <Reference_List>
    <External_Reference>
      <reference_text>Day, M., et al., 2023, A new body of paired CTX and HiRISE DTMs for targets of demonstrated  
                scientific- and human exploration interest, 54th Lunar and Planteary Science Conference, Woodlands, TX. Abstract.
            </reference_text>
      <description>Pairs of overlapping digital terrain models (DTMs) were generated from stereo HiRISE- and CTX
				images to provide detailed and contextual topographic data for areas of demonstrated interest. In particular, 
				this body of DTMs focuses on areas proposed for human exploration in the 2015 NASA HLS2 workshop, and on 
				images targeted in stereo by the HiRISE team. </description>
    </External_Reference>
    <External_Reference>
      <doi>10.1029/2018EA000409</doi>
      <reference_text>Beyer, R. A., Alexandrov, O., McMichael, S., 2018, The Ames Stereo Pipeline: NASA's Open 
                Source Software for Deriving and Processing Terrain Data, Earth and Space Science, 9, 537-548)
            </reference_text>
      <description>The NASA Ames Stereo Pipeline is a suite of free and open source automated geodesy and 
                stereogrammetry tools designed for processing stereo images captured from satellites (around 
                Earth and other planets), robotic rovers, aerial cameras, and historical images, with and 
                without accurate camera pose information.</description>
    </External_Reference>
  </Reference_List>
